# `from` on the right of `join` or `union` is not written there: a generic error until M1-25.
mode: syntax
---- query
from orders | join from customers on customerId;
from orders | union from 'b.csv'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..82
  PIPELINE@0..47
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..11
      IDENT@5..11 "orders"
    WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
    PIPE@12..13 "|"
    WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
    JOIN_OP@14..47
      IDENT@14..18 "join"
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..23 "from"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      NAME_REF@24..33
        IDENT@24..33 "customers"
      WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
      IDENT@34..36 "on"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      NAME_REF@37..47
        IDENT@37..47 "customerId"
  SEMICOLON@47..48 ";"
  WHITESPACE@48..49 "\n"
  PIPELINE@49..81
    IDENT@49..53 "from"
    WHITESPACE@53..54 " "
    NAME_REF@54..60
      IDENT@54..60 "orders"
    WHITESPACE@60..61 " "
    PIPE@61..62 "|"
    WHITESPACE@62..63 " "
    UNION_OP@63..81
      IDENT@63..68 "union"
      WHITESPACE@68..69 " "
      IDENT@69..73 "from"
      WHITESPACE@73..74 " "
      LITERAL@74..81
        STRING@74..81 "'b.csv'"
  WHITESPACE@81..82 "\n"

error[DS0101]: expected a table after `join`, found `from`
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from orders | join from customers on customerId;
  |                    ^^^^ `from` starts a query, not a table here
  |
  = help: write the table directly, or put a pipeline in parentheses: `(from t | take 5)`

error[DS0101]: expected a table after `union`, found `from`
  --> query:2:21
  |
2 | from orders | union from 'b.csv'
  |                     ^^^^ `from` starts a query, not a table here
  |
  = help: write the table directly, or put a pipeline in parentheses: `(from t | take 5)`
